WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.718 --> 00:00:17.339
Ivy couldn't take it anymore.

2
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:23.001
She jumped into the water, and Ezra jumped in after her.

3
00:00:24.442 --> 00:00:25.702
She looked around for Glen.

4
00:00:25.722 --> 00:00:27.623
"Where is he?"

5
00:00:28.083 --> 00:00:29.084
she thought in a panic.

6
00:00:30.348 --> 00:00:32.849
Glen swam to the surface and gasped for air.

7
00:00:36.732 --> 00:00:37.832
thought you drowned!"

8
00:00:38.292 --> 00:00:38.933
Ivy shouted.

9
00:00:38.953 --> 00:00:40.854
"I'm fine.

10
00:00:41.194 --> 00:00:43.775
But those rocks are too heavy," Glen said.

11
00:00:43.795 --> 00:00:45.937
"Our plan won't work."

12
00:00:45.957 --> 00:00:49.799
"You mean, your plan won't work!"

13
00:00:50.339 --> 00:00:50.939
Ivy said.

14
00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.461
Out of the water, the kids grabbed their towels.

15
00:00:54.481 --> 00:00:58.964
"That was a terrible idea, Ezra," Glen said.

16
00:01:00.168 --> 00:01:02.730
"You called it incredible, remember?"

17
00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:03.770
Ezra said.

18
00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:07.372
"Wait—I have the best idea ever!"

19
00:01:07.752 --> 00:01:08.373
Glen said.

20
00:01:08.393 --> 00:01:11.875
"Let's drill holes in the other teams' canoes."

21
00:01:13.135 --> 00:01:14.196
Ivy rolled her eyes.

22
00:01:14.216 --> 00:01:16.917
"Everyone will see the holes."

23
00:01:18.658 --> 00:01:19.439
Glen sighed.

24
00:01:19.459 --> 00:01:21.080
"Oh well.

25
00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:25.382
I guess we'll just have to think about ice cream—and paddle fast!"

26
00:01:27.603 --> 00:01:28.744
It was the day of the race.

27
00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:32.982
Campers lined up by the lake to watch the three teams compete.

28
00:01:34.043 --> 00:01:36.805
The canoers put on life vests and grabbed paddles.

29
00:01:37.986 --> 00:01:39.047
Ivy felt terrible.

30
00:01:39.847 --> 00:01:42.910
But it wasn't just the thought of losing the race that was bothering her.

31
00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:47.413
"I must have caught what Annie had," she said.

32
00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:49.655
"My throat is sore."

33
00:01:51.296 --> 00:01:52.417
Ezra looked concerned.

34
00:01:52.437 --> 00:01:55.078
"Should you go to the infirmary?"

35
00:01:55.999 --> 00:01:56.800
Ivy shook her head.

36
00:01:57.932 --> 00:02:00.094
"Nurse Kramer will never believe me.

37
00:02:01.555 --> 00:02:02.916
I'll get through the race somehow."

38
00:02:02.937 --> 00:02:08.121
"Look, Annie's still not back," Glen said.

39
00:02:08.141 --> 00:02:11.304
"That means we have a chance!"

40
00:02:11.324 --> 00:02:14.547
"You're right," Ezra said.

41
00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:16.348
"We can still win!"

42
00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:18.710
Ivy coughed.

43
00:02:19.911 --> 00:02:21.112
"Let's get this over with.

44
00:02:21.873 --> 00:02:22.654
I need a nap."

45
00:02:22.674 --> 00:02:27.033
"Canoers, take your positions!"

46
00:02:27.453 --> 00:02:28.254
Private shouted.

47
00:02:29.875 --> 00:02:31.416
Everyone climbed into the canoes.

48
00:02:34.037 --> 00:02:35.298
Private blew her whistle.

49
00:02:36.298 --> 00:02:38.860
Blue took the lead, with Red close behind.

50
00:02:40.301 --> 00:02:42.382
The Yellow team's canoe went off to the right.

51
00:02:42.402 --> 00:02:48.265
"What stroke do we use to go straight ahead?"

52
00:02:48.585 --> 00:02:49.286
Ezra asked.

53
00:02:49.306 --> 00:02:51.647
"How should I know?"

54
00:02:51.967 --> 00:02:52.588
Glen said.

55
00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.802
Red and Blue were now halfway across the lake.

56
00:02:57.963 --> 00:02:59.223
They were almost tied.

57
00:03:00.765 --> 00:03:04.667
Ivy and the boys paddled hard, but their canoe kept going in a circle.

58
00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:07.950
They could hear kids laughing from the shore.

59
00:03:09.631 --> 00:03:10.451
Glen groaned.

60
00:03:10.471 --> 00:03:12.833
"This is humiliating."

61
00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:18.037
Blue was ahead, but Red shot forward in the final seconds.

62
00:03:18.057 --> 00:03:21.399
"Yay, Red!"

63
00:03:21.839 --> 00:03:22.660
Campers cheered.

64
00:03:23.952 --> 00:03:25.934
Yellow floated in the middle of the lake.

65
00:03:25.954 --> 00:03:31.138
"We got last place," Ezra said sadly.

66
00:03:31.158 --> 00:03:34.081
"No ice cream for us."

67
00:03:36.022 --> 00:03:37.764
Ivy sneezed twice and groaned.

68
00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:40.306
"Forget the ice cream.

69
00:03:41.707 --> 00:03:43.769
Get me a box of tissues!"

70
00:03:46.311 --> 00:03:49.554
A few days later, a group of campers stood by the camp bus.

71
00:03:50.795 --> 00:03:54.261
A sign on the bus read, Great Job, Sports Day Winners!

72
00:03:55.322 --> 00:03:57.283
The Red canoe team boarded the bus.

73
00:03:57.664 --> 00:04:00.305
Huck climbed on behind them, pumping his fists.

74
00:04:00.325 --> 00:04:06.770
"I scream, you scream, we all scream for ice cream!"

75
00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:08.311
the winners shouted.

76
00:04:09.552 --> 00:04:11.833
The doors closed, and the bus pulled away.

77
00:04:11.853 --> 00:04:15.776
"Those lucky winners," Glen mumbled.

78
00:04:16.877 --> 00:04:17.617
Ezra sighed.

79
00:04:17.637 --> 00:04:21.400
"Time for the soccer game."

80
00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.140
Glen stared at Ivy.

81
00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.681
"Why are you smiling?

82
00:04:27.321 --> 00:04:28.422
You hate soccer.

83
00:04:29.822 --> 00:04:32.283
And you wanted to leave camp to go to Frosty Freeze."

84
00:04:32.303 --> 00:04:37.085
"I showed Larry the drawings for my graphic novel," Ivy said.

85
00:04:37.105 --> 00:04:43.106
"He loved my zombie drawing so much, he paid me ten dollars for it!"

86
00:04:44.947 --> 00:04:47.448
She pulled a bill out of her pocket and waved it around.

87
00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:54.202
"When I'm a famous artist, I'll buy us all the ice cream we can eat."

88
00:04:55.082 --> 00:04:58.364
Just then Chuck and Buck ran by, kicking a soccer ball.

89
00:04:59.544 --> 00:05:00.825
Buck kicked the ball hard.

90
00:05:01.825 --> 00:05:03.846
It sailed through the air and—bonk!

91
00:05:04.506 --> 00:05:05.826
It hit Ivy on the head.

92
00:05:05.846 --> 00:05:09.748
"Ouch!" she cried, still smiling.
